{"type": "root", "attrs": {"type": "node", "context": "cop2", "internal": "tima", "icon": "COP2/tima", "index": "no", "version": null, "namespace": null}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Time Machine"], "extent": [72, 89]}, {"type": "summary", "indent": 0, "text": ["Uses a second input to time warp the first input on a per pixel\nbasis."], "extent": [89, 168]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["This operation uses a second input image to time warp the first input\nsequence on a per pixel basis. The second input image\u2019s luminance is\nused to determine which frame to access in the first input. The 'Black\nPixel Frame' and 'White Pixel Frame' are used to specify the frame range\nthat the luminance values map to."], "extent": [211, 530]}, {"type": "tip_group", "body": [{"type": "tip", "indent": 0, "role": "item", "extent": [530, 535], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Try a Ramp or Noise COP as the second input."], "extent": [535, 585]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Overloading VEX Parameters"], "extent": [27, 60], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["This operator is implemented in VEX, which supports parameter\noverloading. If the first input has a plane which matches an\noperation parameter\u2019s channel name, the input plane will be used as\nthe parameter\u2019s value, effectively overriding it. The overloaded\nparameter is then evaluated from the plane on a per-pixel basis."], "extent": [60, 383]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "em", "text": ["eg."]}, " If the input COP has the following planes:"], "extent": [383, 433]}, {"lang": null, "type": "pre", "indent": 0, "text": ["\nC{r,g,b}\nA\nfogdens\n"], "extent": [433, 460]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["and it is fed into a VEX Fog COP, the fog density will be determined\nat each pixel by the fogdens plane, since the Fog Density\nparameter\u2019s channel name matches the 'fogdens' channel name."], "extent": [460, 649]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Scoping"], "extent": [57, 75], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["This operation may be restricted to certain planes, or\n        components of planes. In addition, the operation may be applied\n        to a subset of frames within the sequence. An image must have\n        both its frame and plane scoped to be modified."], "extent": [75, 338]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Images that are not modified are passed through, which does not\n        take any memory or processing time."], "extent": [338, 455]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Masking"], "extent": [56, 74], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["This operation may be masked, which restricts the operation to\n        an area of the image. The mask may be inverted, brightened or\n        dimmed."], "extent": [74, 233]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The mask input is on the side of the node. The label on the\n        connector indicates the plane being used as a mask."], "extent": [233, 362]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The mask input can also be scaled to fit the output image\u2019s resolution, if they differ. If this node is changing constantly, and the mask is not, it is somewhat faster to put a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/scale", "type": "link", "text": ["Scale COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/scale.html"}, " down to do the resize for the mask image. Otherwise, the scale will occur every time this node cooks."], "extent": [362, 678]}]}, {"level": 1, "id": "parameters", "container": true, "type": "parameters_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [689, 701], "body": [{"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Time Machine"], "extent": [701, 725], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Black Pixel Frame"], "extent": [725, 753], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The frame value that a black pixel represents."], "extent": [790, 849]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/blackframes"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["White Pixel Frame"], "extent": [849, 876], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The frame value that a white pixel represents."], "extent": [913, 973]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Pixels between the black and white will have frame values\n            that are linearly interpolated between the Black Pixel Frame\n            and the White Pixel Frame. Values above white or below black\n            will be extrapolated."], "extent": [973, 1224]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/whiteframes"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Relative to Current Frame"], "extent": [1224, 1259], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If on, the frame value is added to the current frame,\n            making the frame value an offset from the current frame. If\n            off, the frame values represent actual frame numbers."], "extent": [1259, 1463]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Blend Frames"], "extent": [1463, 1485], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If on, fractional frames are computed and pixels from the\n            two nearest frames are linearly blended together to produce\n            the output frame\u2019s pixel."], "extent": [1485, 1665]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Before Start"], "extent": [1665, 1687], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If a filtered frame is before the beginning of the sequence,\n            this determines what frame to use."], "extent": [1687, 1809]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Black"], "extent": [1809, 1828], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["A black frame."], "extent": [1828, 1859]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Cycle"], "extent": [1859, 1878], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Cycle back into the sequence from the end (so 2 frames\n                before the start will use frame 'end-2')."], "extent": [1878, 2007]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Mirror"], "extent": [2007, 2027], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Mirror back into the sequence (so 2 frames before will\n                use frame 'start+2')."], "extent": [2027, 2136]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Hold"], "extent": [2136, 2154], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Use the first frame."], "extent": [2154, 2191]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["After End"], "extent": [2191, 2210], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Similar to 'Before Start', except this parameter determines\n            what frame to use if filtering goes past the last frame of\n            the sequence."], "extent": [2210, 2379]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Scoping"], "extent": [57, 75], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["This operation may be restricted to certain planes, or\n        components of planes. In addition, the operation may be applied\n        to a subset of frames within the sequence. An image must have\n        both its frame and plane scoped to be modified."], "extent": [75, 338]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Images that are not modified are passed through, which does not\n        take any memory or processing time."], "extent": [338, 455]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Masking"], "extent": [56, 74], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["This operation may be masked, which restricts the operation to\n        an area of the image. The mask may be inverted, brightened or\n        dimmed."], "extent": [74, 233]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The mask input is on the side of the node. The label on the\n        connector indicates the plane being used as a mask."], "extent": [233, 362]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The mask input can also be scaled to fit the output image\u2019s resolution, if they differ. If this node is changing constantly, and the mask is not, it is somewhat faster to put a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/scale", "type": "link", "text": ["Scale COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/scale.html"}, " down to do the resize for the mask image. Otherwise, the scale will occur every time this node cooks."], "extent": [362, 678]}]}], "text": "Parameters"}, {"level": 1, "id": "locals", "container": true, "type": "locals_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [2471, 2479], "body": [{"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["L"], "extent": [26, 29], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Sequence length"], "extent": [29, 49]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["S"], "extent": [49, 52], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Start of sequence"], "extent": [52, 74]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["E"], "extent": [74, 77], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["End of sequence"], "extent": [77, 97]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["IL"], "extent": [97, 101], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Input sequence length"], "extent": [101, 127]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["SR"], "extent": [127, 131], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Sequence frame rate"], "extent": [131, 155]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["NP"], "extent": [155, 159], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Number of planes in sequence"], "extent": [159, 192]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["W,H"], "extent": [192, 197], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Width and height of image"], "extent": [197, 227]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["I"], "extent": [227, 230], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Image index (0 at start frame)"], "extent": [230, 265]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["IT"], "extent": [265, 269], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Image time (0 at start frame)"], "extent": [269, 303]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["AI"], "extent": [303, 307], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Current plane array index"], "extent": [307, 337]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["PI"], "extent": [337, 341], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Current plane index"], "extent": [341, 365]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["PC"], "extent": [365, 369], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Num of channels in current plane"], "extent": [369, 406]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CXRES"], "extent": [406, 413], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project X resolution"], "extent": [413, 448]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CYRES"], "extent": [448, 455], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project Y resolution"], "extent": [455, 490]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CPIXA"], "extent": [490, 497], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project pixel aspect ratio"], "extent": [497, 538]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CDEPTH"], "extent": [538, 546], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project raster depth"], "extent": [546, 581]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CBP"], "extent": [581, 586], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project black point"], "extent": [586, 620]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CWP"], "extent": [620, 625], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project white point"], "extent": [625, 659]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "text": "Locals"}, {"level": 1, "id": "related", "container": true, "type": "related_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [2505, 2514], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/warp", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/warp.html"}], "extent": [2514, 2537]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/timefilter", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/timefilter.html"}], "extent": [2537, 2566]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/timescale", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/timescale.html"}], "extent": [2566, 2594]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/shift", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/shift.html"}], "extent": [2594, 2618]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/trim", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/trim.html"}], "extent": [2618, 2642]}], "container": true}], "text": "Related"}], "title": ["Time Machine"], "summary": ["Uses a second input to time warp the first input on a per pixel\nbasis."], "included": ["/composite/_old_cops_deprecated", "/nodes/cop2/localvars", "/nodes/cop2/maskparms", "/nodes/cop2/pixelparms", "/nodes/cop2/vexnode"]}